# s4_dealerbuf_measured
#
# donor      BumbleBee b4_slice_budget_64m; this line's s2, s3 (hardcoded reservation corrected
#            against measured need).
# basis      s3_keybuf_measured host peak:
#              21474.8 MB  95.0%  heap:sigma.cu:248:main  <- gpu_mem.cu:77:cpuMalloc
#                547.6 MB   2.4%  heap:bert.h:89:GPUBERT<unsigned long>::GPUBERT
#            20 GiB = three pinned allocations from one constructor:
#              keyBuf      18 GiB   sized by s3 against a measured 16.83 GiB
#              llamaBuf1    1 GiB   <- this step
#              dummyBuf1    1 GiB   <- this step
#            cpuMalloc(size_t, bool pin = true) -> cudaHostRegister: every reserved page resident.
# need       probe off-path-runs/p_llamabuf_highwater/ (job 46142898):
#              SNNI_BUF|llamabuf_high=281856|llamabuf_alloc=1073741824      275 KiB of 1 GiB, factor 3810
#              SNNI_BUF|dummybuf_used=6764544|dummybuf_alloc=1073741824    6.45 MiB of 1 GiB, factor  159
#            initDealer (backend/sigma.h:302): llamaBuf2 drained and reset per layernorm round (needs
#            max(llamaKeySz)); dummyBuf2 assigned once, never reset (needs sum(llamaKeySz)).
#
# impl_lever: patches/patch_llamabuf_highwater.py patches/patch_dealerbuf_measured.py
# Lever = second file. First = p_llamabuf_highwater probe, applied before it (reporting only),
# carried by this binary.
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: main
# cost_class: free
#
# name       `main` = grouped-table name (finer: sigma.cu:248:main), as in s3.
# lever      both cpuMalloc(OneGB) in the SIGMAKeygen constructor -> 64 MiB (238x the largest round,
#            10x the whole-run sum; same figure as s2's comm buffer).
# margin     chosen assuming no bounds check (offsets by pointer subtraction after writing).
#            Correction 2026-08-15: close() ends with assert(keySize < keyBufSize), live in the binary
#            (NDEBUG not defined), run before the online phase: overflow corrupts the heap, then
#            aborts. Margin more conservative than needed; measurement unaffected.
# free       oversized reservation; pinning 128 MiB is less work than 2 GiB.
# measured   n=1 (replicates: 1, MANIFEST), job 46143085:
#              peak host   22,069,572 -> 20,101,296 kB   -1,968,276 kB   -8.92%
#              runtime             29 s wall
#              gate        T1s, bit-identical to s3
#            predicted 1,966,080 kB, measured 1,968,276 kB (0.11%).
# log note   the probe's alloc fields print a literal 1073741824 (probe applied before this patch);
#            s4's log reports llamabuf_alloc=1073741824 while 64 MiB is allocated. used fields are
#            correct; no derivation uses alloc.
